Rotating imbalance, critical speed and machine loads (@mech-imbalance: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Engineering-Dynamics-MIT-2-003SC.lingua#r_37MSK6EJHRV95GXWA23P4ZJPZ3", #source "../sources/Classical-Dynamics-David-Tong.lingua#r_2M330E943Q98XH7BJKXETRWKNA", #mechanical-engineering "Distributed-mass-stiffness-and-continuous-vibration.lingua#r_7FBSCQHXNQGXNV81TKQ4ZWKCZ4") { r_4EY3NN0859SB8AATY9X5DN5BGK
**Study:** [Engineering Dynamics — MIT 2.003SC, Fall 2011](../sources/Engineering-Dynamics-MIT-2-003SC.lingua#r_37MSK6EJHRV95GXWA23P4ZJPZ3), lecture 9 and recitation 6, followed by lectures 20–26; [Classical Dynamics — David Tong](../sources/Classical-Dynamics-David-Tong.lingua#r_2M330E943Q98XH7BJKXETRWKNA), rigid-body kinematics and inertia. Return to the machine's actual support and shaft geometry.

A mass m_e at eccentricity e rotating at constant angular speed Ω produces a rotating inertial-force demand with magnitude m_e e Ω² in the simple rigid-rotor model. Static unbalance and couple unbalance require different correction information; balancing one plane does not automatically correct a two-plane rotor.

An unbalance product of 0.0001 kg·m at 3000 rpm gives force magnitude about 9.8696 N. The rotor's displacement also depends on support stiffness, damping, mode shape and speed. Force increasing as Ω² does not imply displacement increasing as Ω² throughout a resonance crossing.

A simple flexible-rotor model can have a critical speed near a lateral natural frequency. Gyroscopic terms, asymmetric supports, spin-dependent properties, internal damping and rubbing can change the frequencies and stability. A single stationary oscillator is an introduction, not a certificate for an arbitrary rotor's permissible speed.

**Work:** Predict the response to a known unbalance in a declared one-mode model and sweep speed through its resonance. Separate shaft motion, bearing force and casing motion. Compare run-up and settled assumptions, include phase relative to shaft angle, and state what additional measurements would distinguish unbalance from misalignment or a loosened support. Actual high-speed balancing and overspeed tests need appropriate facilities and procedures.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
